  Full 9-chapter curriculum elevated to University Rigor:
  1. First-Order Differential Equations, Separable Equations & Existence Theory (Picard-Lindelöf)
  2. Linear First-Order Equations, Integrating Factors & Nonlinear Reductions (Bernoulli & Riccati)
  3. Second-Order Linear Homogeneous Equations, Auxiliary Roots & Wronskian Theory (Abel's Identity)
  4. Nonhomogeneous Equations, Undetermined Coefficients & Resonance (Annihilator Method)
  5. Variation of Parameters, Wronskian Systems & Green's Kernel (Cauchy Impulse Response)
  6. The Laplace Transform, Discontinuous Forcing & Convolution Theory (Volterra Equations)
  7. Systems of Linear Differential Equations, Phase Plane Topology & Matrix Exponentials
  8. Power Series Solutions, Ordinary Points & the Method of Frobenius (Bessel & Hermite)
  9. Numerical Methods: Euler, Improved Euler (RK2), RK4 & Numerical Stability (Stiff ODEs)

  Features 5 interactive canvas explorers (odeSlopeCanvas, odeLinearCanvas, odeAuxCanvas, odeSysCanvas, odeEulerCanvas)
  and 25 university-rigor free-response problems with complete step-by-step proofs and analytical solutions.
#}
